- Web interface
    - I don't like the plain Enter key to send the message.  I should be able to modify
      it to be e.g. ctrl-Enter; this would let me enter multiline text, which is very
      common for programming-related tasks.
    - The interface is poor for going back and finding stuff.  There should be a menu
      entry that lets me export the text to a file, both for archiving and being able to
      look something up in a terminal window with my editor (browsers are horrible for
      this).  This problem gets worse and worse as the conversation thread gets larger.
- One thing I don't like about Gemini's web interface is I can't modify the user
  interface.  As soon as you hit the Enter key, your message is sent.  You have to use
  shift-Enter if you want a new line.  Particularly for programming, this should be an
  editor style widget.  My only defense is to edit my message outside of the browser,
  then copy & paste in inside the browswer.
- Strengths
    - Google is trying to move towards a collaborator model for the AI rather than just
      a semantic helper.  Mike clearly tries to work this way, especially when asked and
      prompted carefully.  
    - I've been using Mike's help for about 11 days.  We've shared an enormous amount of
      text and messages over that period.  
